{
  "note": "The built-in earlier baseball seasons: each MLB The Show edition's Live series at its last roster update, read from the game's public API (npm run sync:mlb-the-show -- --edition=<nn> writes scripts/data/mlb-the-show-<nn>.json). npm run build:mlb-seasons builds each season's clubs and nations; npm run build:mlb-map builds each era's map from these teams and ballparks. `teams` lists, by The Show's code, the eras in which a franchise played under another name or in another ballpark than today's (scripts/data/mlb-teams.json): such an era keeps today's id, name, code, city and home unless it names its own. `unreliableBirthplaces` names the editions whose birthplaces the build does not trust. Editions 18 to 20 have no API left (their mlb18–mlb20 hosts are gone): their snapshots are ShowZone's copy of the same cards (`showzone`, npm run import:mlb-showzone). ShowZone keeps no older edition's cards, so 2018 is the first season.",
  "source": { "name": "MLB The Show", "provider": "San Diego Studio", "docs": "https://mlb26.theshow.com/apis/docs" },
  "showzone": {
    "note": "MLB The Show 18, 19 and 20 as ShowZone keeps them (docs/design/baseball.md, \"Earlier seasons\"). npm run import:mlb-showzone writes scripts/data/mlb-the-show-18.json to -20.json from ShowZone's answers, cached in the ignored data-src/showzone/ and each pinned here by SHA-256 (`sha256`), and never fetches. `control` is the edition also read as a check against Sony's own API. `provenance` and each edition's `checks` are copied into its snapshot.",
    "compiler": "ShowZone",
    "site": "https://showzone.gg",
    "api": "https://data.showzone.gg/api/players",
    "retrieved": "2026-11-08",
    "control": 2021,
    "provenance": "Sony's own API for this edition is gone. ShowZone (showzone.gg), a fan-run card database that is not the publisher, keeps every Live card of the edition at its last roster update and serves them from a public data API (data.showzone.gg), read once on 2026-11-08: 74 pages of 100 cards, MLB The Show 18 to 21. showzone.gg's robots.txt disallows /api on its own host; the data host serves no robots.txt. ShowZone states 'All Rights Reserved' and publishes no terms; as with Sony's own data, the rights are not cleared. Its MLB The Show 21 equals Sony's own API (scripts/data/mlb-the-show-21.json) on all 2,092 cards, uuid, name, team, position, overall and birthplace, though ShowZone keeps no secondary positions for that edition; its team ids are named by that edition's codes and teams, which the clubs kept from 2018 to 2021.",
    "editions": {
      "2018": { "game": 8, "pages": 16, "rosterUpdate": { "id": 10021, "name": "11-01-2018", "date": "2018-11-01", "url": "https://mlb18.theshownation.com/roster_updates/10021" },
        "checks": "Checked against Sony's own pages in the Wayback Machine: ShowZone holds the new overall and the team of all 37 changes of the last roster update (11-01-2018), and the overall of all 60 MLB 18 cards whose page was captured. ShowZone keeps no birthplace and no secondary position for any MLB 18 card; Sony's MLB 18 card pages show no secondary positions either." },
      "2019": { "game": 7, "pages": 17, "rosterUpdate": { "id": 27, "name": "September 27, 2019", "date": "2019-09-27", "url": "https://mlb19.theshownation.com/roster_updates/27" },
        "checks": "Checked against Sony's own pages in the Wayback Machine: ShowZone holds the new overall and the team of 142 of the 143 changes of the last roster update (September 27, 2019); the other is Giovanny Gallegos (Cardinals, 82), the one Live card ShowZone lacks. The 10 Live cards whose page was captured agree on overall, secondary positions and birthplace." },
      "2020": { "game": 6, "pages": 20, "rosterUpdate": { "id": 18, "name": "October 30, 2020", "date": "2020-10-30", "url": "https://mlb20.theshow.com/roster_updates/18" },
        "checks": "Checked against Sony's own pages: ShowZone holds the new overall and the team of 113 of the 114 changes of the last roster update (October 30, 2020, in the Wayback Machine); the other is Paolo Espino (a free agent, 55), the one Live card ShowZone lacks. The 95 Live cards whose page Common Crawl (93) or the Wayback Machine (2) captured after that update agree on overall, secondary positions and birthplace." },
      "2021": { "game": 5, "pages": 21 }
    },
